<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's Dec import prices down 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's Dec import prices down 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's import prices fell 0.6 percent in December from the previous month, and were 7.3 percent lower than a year before, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;An increase in the value of the Australian dollar against the major trading currencies led to price falls in a range of items in December,&quot; the bureau said.</p>
<p>Import prices fell or remained flat in every month of 1996.</p>
<p>The annual rate of import price inflation has remained between minus 6.1 percent and minus 9.7 percent since May.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
